WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:07.310
Tomas and John were hiking in a forest.

2
00:00:07.311 --> 00:00:11.782
"We have been friends for many years," Tomas said.

3
00:00:11.783 --> 00:00:16.450
"Yes, we have." John smiled.

4
00:00:16.451 --> 00:00:21.856
"Ever since we were children!"

5
00:00:21.857 --> 00:00:26.726
Tomas was lucky because he had made a fortune.

6
00:00:26.727 --> 00:00:31.137
Now he lived in a mansion.

7
00:00:31.138 --> 00:00:37.229
Meanwhile John was poor and lived in a small cabin.

8
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:43.187
"I think your family needs a new house," Tomas said.

9
00:00:43.188 --> 00:00:49.668
"Of course we do, but we are too poor," John said.

10
00:00:49.669 --> 00:00:53.716
"Please let me help you build a new house," Tomas said.

11
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:56.926
"I've had good luck, and I want to share it."

12
00:00:56.927 --> 00:01:00.273
"Thank you, Tomas," John said.

13
00:01:00.274 --> 00:01:04.879
"That sounds wonderful. You're a true friend!"

14
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.535
The friends continued hiking.

15
00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:14.473
As they climbed up a hill, they spotted a bear.

16
00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:18.328
The bear growled and began running toward them.

17
00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:23.247
John was a fast runner.

18
00:01:23.248 --> 00:01:27.797
Leaving Tomas behind, he ran as fast as he could.

19
00:01:27.798 --> 00:01:31.283
He raced up a tall tree.

20
00:01:31.284 --> 00:01:35.997
But Tomas froze in fear.

21
00:01:35.998 --> 00:01:40.174
The bear was coming closer and closer!

22
00:01:40.175 --> 00:01:45.758
"It's no use," Tomas thought. "This bear will eat me!"

23
00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:48.750
Suddenly Tomas had an idea.

24
00:01:48.751 --> 00:01:52.488
"Bears might not eat dead people," he thought.

25
00:01:52.489 --> 00:01:56.096
So Tomas lay down on the ground and held his breath.

26
00:01:56.097 --> 00:02:02.691
He tried to lie very still.

27
00:02:02.692 --> 00:02:06.594
"Please don't eat me. Please!" Tomas thought.

28
00:02:06.595 --> 00:02:09.785
John nervously watched from the tree.

29
00:02:09.786 --> 00:02:14.316
The bear sniffed Tomas, but Tomas did not move.

30
00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:18.435
The bear looked at Tomas closely and then licked his ear.

31
00:02:18.436 --> 00:02:21.198
Tomas still did not move.

32
00:02:21.199 --> 00:02:27.005
At last the bear walked away.

33
00:02:27.006 --> 00:02:32.323
John climbed down and ran to Tomas.

34
00:02:32.324 --> 00:02:36.854
"Whew!" John said. "We're both safe.

35
00:02:36.855 --> 00:02:39.896
Thank goodness the bear didn't hurt you!"

36
00:02:39.897 --> 00:02:43.086
Tomas looked away.

37
00:02:43.087 --> 00:02:47.081
"Right. The bear didn't hurt me," he said coldly.

38
00:02:47.082 --> 00:02:50.251
John was surprised by his friend's cold tone.

39
00:02:50.252 --> 00:02:53.610
"You should be happy, Tomas. You're alive!"

40
00:02:53.611 --> 00:02:57.137
Tomas shrugged. "I guess so."

41
00:02:57.138 --> 00:03:02.287
"Huh?" John thought. "Why is Tomas so upset?"

42
00:03:02.288 --> 00:03:04.498
"Were you scared, Tomas?

43
00:03:04.499 --> 00:03:06.473
I saw the bear lick your ear.

44
00:03:06.474 --> 00:03:09.437
You probably thought it was about to eat you!"

45
00:03:09.438 --> 00:03:14.571
Tomas frowned. "Yes, John. The bear licked my ear.

46
00:03:14.572 --> 00:03:17.041
But it also whispered something.

47
00:03:17.042 --> 00:03:19.578
It said, 'Your friend ran away.

48
00:03:19.579 --> 00:03:23.642
A true friend always stays nearby and helps.'"

49
00:03:23.643 --> 00:03:27.293
John was stunned.

50
00:03:27.294 --> 00:03:32.433
As Tomas walked away alone, John felt sad and ashamed.

51
00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.980
He had thought only of himself.

52
00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:39.383
Now he had lost his friend forever.

53
00:03:39.384 --> 00:03:45.907
As the bear said, a true friend always stays nearby and helps.

